course: dictionary
lesson: 11981
title: The balance brain
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The cerebellum is a part of your brain. It sits at the back, under the big main part of the brain. Its job is to help you keep your balance, move smoothly and coordinate your body, so your arms, legs and eyes work together.
explain: Think about riding a bike. You do not have to think hard about every wobble, because your cerebellum helps you stay upright. «The cerebellum controls balance» means it is the part that keeps you from falling over when you move.
explain: Science words often look hard, but you can break them down. Cerebellum comes from Latin and means "little brain". When you meet the word, read the sentence around it: the clues tell you what the part does, even if the word is new.
fact: The cerebellum is the part of the brain at the back, under the big main part.
fact: The cerebellum controls balance, smooth movement and coordination.
fact: When you ride a bike, walk or catch a ball, the cerebellum helps your body work together.
fact: «Cerebellum» is a noun. Its plural can be «cerebellums» or «cerebella».
fact: Damage to the cerebellum can make movement and balance harder.
exercise: «The cerebellum helps Maya keep her balance on the beam.» What does the cerebellum control? | Remembering your birthday | Hearing sounds from far away | Your favourite colour | *Balance and smooth movement
exercise: Where is the cerebellum? | *At the back of the brain, under the big main part | At the front of the face, behind the nose | In the stomach, near the food | At the very tip of the fingers
exercise: «Ben's cerebellum helps him catch the ball.» What does the cerebellum help Ben do? | Taste his lunch | Hear the crowd cheering | Read a long book | *Catch the ball smoothly
test: «Damage to the cerebellum can make walking hard.» Which ability does the cerebellum affect here? | *Balance and walking | Breathing in the night | Seeing colours | Remembering stories
test: Which word means the same kind of job as coordination for the cerebellum? | Sneezing | Digesting your lunch | *Moving your body parts together | Growing taller
exam: Leo says the cerebellum is in his knee. Why is he wrong? | It is in the ears, and nowhere else | *It is in the brain, at the back | It is in the knee, next to the bone | It is in the blood, moving round the body
